          "parts": [
            "Based on public information, Saintly Skin appears to be a founder-led medical aesthetics practice rather than a private equity-backed or franchise operation. Here's what I found about the ownership and leadership.\n\n## Owner & Founder\n\n\ue200entity\ue202[\"people\",\"Megan Naccari\",\"Owner and esthetician at Saintly Skin\"]\ue201\n\nMegan is the founder and owner of Saintly Skin in Metairie, Louisiana. According to the company's website:\n\n- Native of New Orleans\n- Graduate of Ridgewood Preparatory School (Metairie)\n- Licensed esthetician trained at John Jay Beauty College in Kenner\n- Founded Saintly Skin around 2016\n- Built the practice from an esthetics-focused business into a full-service medical aesthetics practice\n- Positions herself as combining technical aesthetic knowledge with a highly relationship-driven patient experience. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\n### What she appears to specialize in\n\nFrom the practice website and marketing:\n\n- Acne treatment\n- Anti-aging treatments\n- Skin rejuvenation\n- Medical-grade skincare\n- Advanced facial treatments\n- Building customized treatment plans rather than one-off services \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search7\ue201\n\n---\n\n## Medical Partner / Clinical Leadership\n\n\ue200entity\ue202[\"people\",\"Brittani Naccari Farrell\",\"Family Nurse Practitioner at Saintly Skin\"]\ue201\n\nOne thing that stands out is that Brittani shares the Naccari surname, suggesting she is likely related to Megan (possibly sisters, though I couldn't verify that publicly).\n\nHer background is considerably more medical:\n\n- BSN from LSU Health Sciences Center\n- MSN Family Nurse Practitioner from University of Louisiana Lafayette\n- Board-certified FNP\n- Florence Nightingale Rookie of the Year recipient\n- Injector certifications in:\n  - Botox\n  - Dysport\n  - Xeomin\n  - Dermal fillers\n  - PDO threads\n- Former cardiology nurse before moving into aesthetics. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\nThis combination of owner-esthetician plus nurse practitioner is a fairly common and effective ownership model for successful medical spas.\n\n---\n\n## Medical Director\n\n\ue200entity\ue202[\"people\",\"Susan Julius\",\"Medical Director at Saintly Skin\"]\ue201\n\nTheir physician oversight comes from Dr. Susan Julius.\n\nShe has an unusually strong r\u00e9sum\u00e9:\n\n- Family Medicine\n- Addiction Medicine\n- Physical Therapy background\n- Speaker and educator\n- Media appearances\n- Ochsner residency\n- Case Western medical degree \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\n---\n\n## Other Leadership\n\nAdditional providers include:\n\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"people\",\"Sharee Encalade Marconi\",\"Nurse Practitioner at Saintly Skin\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"people\",\"Penny Bergeron\",\"Registered Nurse at Saintly Skin\"]\ue201\n\nThe practice appears provider-heavy, which generally indicates they're focused on injectables and medical aesthetics rather than being primarily an esthetics salon. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\n---\n\n# Business Snapshot\n\nAccording to LinkedIn and their website:\n\n- Founded: approximately **2016**\n- Headquarters: Metairie, Louisiana\n- Company size: roughly **2\u201310 employees** (LinkedIn estimate)\n- Serves New Orleans, Metairie, Mandeville, Covington, and surrounding Louisiana markets\n- Positioned as a premium medical spa offering injectables, lasers, skin treatments, and weight-loss services. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search7\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\n---\n\n# Brand Positioning\n\nTheir messaging is notably different from many \"Botox-first\" med spas.\n\nInstead they emphasize:\n\n- Education first\n- Comprehensive consultations\n- Home skincare regimens\n- Long-term skin health\n- Medical-grade products\n- Relationship-driven care\n\nThis is a fairly mature positioning strategy that tends to attract higher-value patients rather than discount shoppers. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\n---\n\n# What They Appear to Do Well\n\nFrom reviewing their public presence:\n\n**Strengths**\n- Strong founder branding around Megan.\n- Professional, modern website.\n- Heavy emphasis on consultations instead of transactions.\n- Good mix of esthetic and medical expertise.\n- Broad treatment portfolio (injectables, lasers, skincare, weight loss).\n- Financing options (Cherry) and membership offerings, which can improve patient retention. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search7\ue201\n\n---\n\n# Potential Business Opportunities\n\nLooking at them through the lens of a growth consultancy like yours, I see several areas where they could potentially benefit:\n\n- More systematic patient retention and lifetime value optimization.\n- Membership and recurring-revenue expansion.\n- Advanced referral systems.\n- Multi-location growth planning (if that's part of their long-term vision).\n- Backend revenue optimization beyond acquiring new patients.\n- Operational systems and marketing automation.\n\nThey already appear to have competent branding and clinical credibility, so the biggest opportunities would likely be in scaling revenue and patient lifetime value rather than fixing a weak public image.\n\nOverall, Megan Naccari comes across as a founder who has built the practice around her personal reputation and clinical philosophy, while partnering with experienced nurse practitioners and a seasoned medical director to support a comprehensive medical aesthetics offering. The business appears established, professionally run, and well positioned within the New Orleans market. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search7\ue201"
          ]
